{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Large Phase 3A batch translation task: replace `todo!()` stub bodies in 6 Rust test files with faithful translations of the corresponding C test bodies from `picoquictest/`. The 6 files are:\n   - `ticket_store_test.c` → `rs/fq/src/tests/ticket_store.rs` (5 tests)\n   - `tls_api_test.c` → `rs/fq/src/tests/tls_api.rs` (177 tests)\n   - `transport_param_test.c` → `rs/fq/src/tests/transport_param.rs` (4 tests)\n   - `util_test.c` → `rs/fq/src/tests/util_test.rs` (already largely translated; 3 remaining stubs already pass the check)\n   - `warptest.c` → `rs/fq/src/tests/warptest.rs` (5 tests)\n   - `wifitest.c` → `rs/fq/src/tests/wifitest.rs` (14 tests)\n\n   Key constraints:\n   - A test is considered \"translated\" when its `#[test] fn` body is ANYTHING other than the bare auto-stub: `#[test]\\nfn <name>() {\\n    todo!(\"<entry_fn>\")\\n}`\n   - Tests don't need to pass — they can panic naturally inside `todo!()` implementations\n   - New helpers that don't exist must be added as `todo!()` stubs in `rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs` or `rs/fq/src/lib.rs`/`rs/fq/src/internal.rs`\n   - No `unsafe` code; no edits outside `rs/fq/src/tests/`, `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`, or the stub-addition locations\n   - Build gate: `cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`\n   - Verification: `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py <src>` after each file\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Phase 3A stub detection pattern**: `#\\[test\\]\\s*\\n\\s*fn\\s+<name>\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*\\{\\s*todo!\\s*\\(\\s*\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"\\s*\\)\\s*\\n?\\s*\\}` — any other body counts as translated\n   - **`fugit` time types**: `Instant<u64, 1, 1_000_000>` constructed via `Instant::from_ticks(usec)`\n   - **`PICOQUIC_INTERNAL_TEST_VERSION_1`** = `0x50435130` = `Version::InternalTest1 as u32`\n   - **`TestTlsApiCtx`**: has `pub qclient: Box<Quic>`, `pub qserver: Box<Quic>`, `pub c_to_s_link`, `pub s_to_c_link`\n   - **`tls_api_init_ctx`** returns `Option<Box<TestTlsApiCtx>>` (itself `todo!()`)\n   - **`ZeroRttTest`** C fields: `use_badcrypt`, `hardreset`, `early_loss`, `no_coal`, `long_data`, `extra_delay`, `do_multipath`, `propose_ech`, `change_params`\n   - **`WarptestSpec`**: `ccalgo_id: Option<&'static str>`, `do_audio`, `do_video`, `data_size`, `datagram_data_size`, `max_streams_client/server`, `max_stream_data`, `bandwidth`\n   - **`WifiTestSpec`**: `latency`, `suspension: &'static [WifiTestSuspension]`, `ccalgo_id: &'static str`, `cc_algo_option`, `target_time`, `simulate_receive_block`, `queue_max_delay`\n   - **`WifiTestSuspension`**: `suspend_time: u64`, `suspend_interval: u64`\n   - Wifi test IDs (C enum): RENO=0, CUBIC=1, BBR=2, RENO_HARD=3, CUBIC_HARD=4, BBR_HARD=5, RENO_LONG=6, CUBIC_LONG=7, BBR_LONG=8, BBR_SHADOW=9, BBR_MANY=10, BBR1=11, BBR1_HARD=12, BBR1_LONG=13\n   - **`tls_api_one_scenario_body`** signature: `(ctx, time, scenario: &[TestApiStreamDesc], init_loss_mask, _cwin_blocked, _proposed_version, _max_sim_time_microsec, max_completion_microsec)`\n   - **`tls_api_connection_loop`** signature: `(ctx, loss_mask: &mut u64, queue_delay_max, simulated_time)`\n   - **`PacketType`** enum: Error, VersionNegotiation, Initial, Retry, Handshake, ZeroRttProtected, OneRttProtected, TypeMax\n   - Quic methods already in `internal.rs`: `store_ticket`, `get_ticket`, `get_stored_ticket`, `load_tickets`, `save_tickets`, `store_token`, `get_token`, `save_tokens`, `load_tokens`, `registered_token_check_reuse`, `registered_token_clear`\n   - `set_default_tp_value(id: u64, value: u64)` already exists in `lib.rs`\n   - `TEST_SNI = \"test.example.com\"`, `TEST_ALPN = \"picoquic-test\"` in util.rs\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs`** — Modified in two places\n     - **Updated `ZeroRttTest` struct** (was wrong, now matches actual C `zero_rtt_test_t`):\n       ```rust\n       #[derive(Default)]\n       pub struct ZeroRttTest {\n           pub use_badcrypt: bool,\n           pub hardreset: bool,\n           pub early_loss: u64,\n           pub no_coal: bool,\n           pub long_data: bool,\n           pub extra_delay: u64,\n           pub do_multipath: bool,\n           pub propose_ech: bool,\n           pub change_params: bool,\n       }\n       ```\n     - **Appended large block of new helper stubs** at the end (after line 1107), including:\n       ```rust\n       pub fn tls_api_loss_test(_loss_mask: u64) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn tls_api_test_with_loss(_ticket_file: Option<&str>, _proposed_version: u32, _sni: Option<&str>, _alpn: Option<&str>) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn session_resume_test_one(_ticket_file: &str) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn mtu_discovery_test_one(_policy: u32, _mtu_expected_client: u32, _mtu_expected_server: u32, _target_time: u64, _mtu_max: u32) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn mtu_drop_cc_algotest(_algo_id: &'static str, _target_time: u64) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn stop_sending_test_one(_discard: bool, _reset_loss: bool) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn transmit_cnxid_test_one(_retire_before: bool, _disable: bool, _early: bool) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn nat_rebinding_test_one(_loss_mask: u64, _cid_zero: bool, _latency: u64) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn migration_test_scenario(_scenario: &[TestApiStreamDesc], _loss_mask: u64, _cid_zero: bool) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn migration_controlled_test_one(_mode: u32) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn padding_test_one(_padding_multiple: u32, _padding_min_size: u32) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n       pub fn qlog_trace_test_one(_recv_ecn: u8, _parallel